  "visualBrief": "Specific Capela dos Ossos interior and connected São Francisco exterior envelope: traversable entry vestibule/stone portal, three-aisle hall with eight bone-covered piers, pale groin vaults/ribs and original simplified ceiling scrolls, dense original skull/long-bone wall vocabulary, high side openings, dark/pale banded floor and simplified gilded twisted-column altar/cross. Host includes mapped stone nave/pointed west portico, crenellated gable/parapets and conical corner pinnacles, connected white lower ranges/shared tiled roofs. Chapel is an interior allocation inside the named host, not a separate building shell. No copied religious painting, readable inscription or photographic bone atlas; no full host church/museum interior.",
