  "sourceFacts": {
    "horizontalBasis": "Exact-QID Capela dos Ossos node6763794307/Q2561983 and named standard PMTiles museum point17598949838723 lie in mapped São Francisco host control35184534465311; host name is corroborated by PMTiles church point35184534465311. No separate chapel footprint/interior map exists. Anchor-7.9083714,38.5687532; heading0, internal local+x angle-.19rad follows host axes. Chapel is allocated approximately within the connected southern wing: room11x20.5m along local+z, altar south/local+z, entry via north vestibule and west courtyard access. Internal station/facing allocation is explicitly approximate, not a surveyed interior. Replace the one complete host control while retaining every independent neighboring building.",
    "architecturalHeights": "Ordinary-picture/map visualization estimates, not surveys: host nave approximately58x22m/eave21.5m/ridge25.2m, west five-bay pointed portico around5.7m deep/7m high, crenellated front/parapet and small conical corner pinnacles. Lower host ranges7.5-9m/eaves with red tiled roofs. Chapel clear room11x20.5m, pier spring3.35m/vault crown5.9m, eight round piers in two rows/five longitudinal bays, original skull/bone and ceiling motif allocations. Vestibule/portal access, exact columns/vault/room dimensions, unseen roofs and ornament inventory remain approximations."
  },
